Hi Felipe,

Without more information about the data and the exact code you are using to
impute it, it is hard to know what is happening. It could be the case that
the NAs in your data are not coded correctly and therefore not recognized as
missing by R. You can check this by using:

sum(is.na(a.out$imputations[[1]]))

This code will tell you how many missing observations there are in the
(supposedly) imputed dataset. This number might be greater than zero if you
tagged certain variables as "idvars"---these variables are not imputed.

Cheers,
matt.

