Hi Felipe,

The problem with the data you are using is that there are rows that are
completely missing. That is, there is no observed information for those
rows. Amelia cannot impute rows with no observed data, so it returns those
rows with all NAs. There is a warning message about this when you run
Amelia, but you may have missed it at the beginning of the imputation
procedure.

Cheers,
matt.

